{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37130558",
      "title": "Styling Buttons & Working with Padding",
      "lectureOrder": 47,
      "videoOrder": 44,
      "sourceHash": "745ba3f4ade4074fabb2b1df788480f995e7a9cc24bf14105a381d6690b56086",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "So let's fix the styling of this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "For that, I'd like to make sure that it's back in the center",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 9.933,
          "en": "and this button also should look differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.92,
          "end": 12.69,
          "en": "Now, regarding the center part,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 15.27,
          "en": "it's of course strange that it's not in the center",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.27,
          "end": 18.21,
          "en": "because it's still inside of that center widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.21,
          "end": 20.01,
          "en": "But here it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.01,
          "end": 22.74,
          "en": "that this column widget by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.74,
          "end": 26.91,
          "en": "takes all the available vertical space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.91,
          "end": 30.15,
          "en": "It is indeed centered horizontally, as you can see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.15,
          "end": 31.98,
          "en": "It's in the center regarding that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.98,
          "end": 33,
          "en": "But vertically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33,
          "end": 35.97,
          "en": "column simply takes the entire available space,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.97,
          "end": 37.47,
          "en": "and therefore there, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.47,
          "end": 40.95,
          "en": "is simply no way of centering it vertically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.95,
          "end": 44.28,
          "en": "So in order to make sure that this is centered vertically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.28,
          "end": 45.69,
          "en": "we must make sure that column",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 49.05,
          "en": "does not take the entire vertical space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.05,
          "end": 51.87,
          "en": "And this can be done with help of another argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 51.87,
          "end": 53.31,
          "en": "that can be set on column.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.31,
          "end": 56.46,
          "en": "And that's the main axis size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.46,
          "end": 60.06,
          "en": "The main axis for a column is simply the vertical axis.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.06,
          "end": 62.43,
          "en": "And here you got two main options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.43,
          "end": 66.72,
          "en": "MainAxisSize.min, and MainAxisSize.max.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 66.72,
          "end": 69.81,
          "en": "These are two predefined values which you can use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 69.81,
          "end": 73.65,
          "en": "and the default is max to take as much space as possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.65,
          "end": 75.741,
          "en": "Here, we therefore want min.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.741,
          "end": 78,
          "en": "And with that, if you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 79.833,
          "en": "this is centered vertically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 83.73,
          "en": "Now, for the styling of the button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 85.53,
          "en": "we of course also wanna change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 85.53,
          "end": 89.52,
          "en": "And that can be done by adding the style argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 89.52,
          "end": 91.2,
          "en": "to the text button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 94.25999999999999,
          "en": "And actually you should move that in front of child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 96.45,
          "en": "not because you technically need to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 96.45,
          "end": 98.58,
          "en": "but because that is one of the patterns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 98.58,
          "end": 100.22999999999999,
          "en": "recommended by Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.22999999999999,
          "end": 102.963,
          "en": "to always keep your widget arguments last.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.16,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "Now, style here wants a button style value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "And the easiest way of creating this for a text button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 113.973,
          "en": "is to use TextButton.styleFrom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 119.55,
          "en": "That's the end of function defined on this text button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.55,
          "end": 122.13,
          "en": "which returns a button style object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.13,
          "end": 124.86,
          "en": "And styleFrom now takes various arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.86,
          "end": 128.28,
          "en": "which you can use to overwrite the default styling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.28,
          "end": 130.92,
          "en": "For example, you can set the foreground color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.92,
          "end": 133.02,
          "en": "to change the default text color,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.02,
          "end": 135.66,
          "en": "because the foreground color of a text button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.66,
          "end": 137.643,
          "en": "is the text color in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.63,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "And here you could set this to colors.white,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "using this predefined color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 147.18,
          "en": "You can also add a separate text style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147.18,
          "end": 149.64,
          "en": "which then wants a text style object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 152.49,
          "en": "using this text style constructor function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.49,
          "end": 156.06,
          "en": "which we already before used for styling the text widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 156.06,
          "end": 157.773,
          "en": "So this constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 158.94,
          "end": 161.64,
          "en": "And there we could also set the text color,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 161.64,
          "end": 165.513,
          "en": "but I'll just use it for setting the font size to 28 here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 166.92000000000002,
          "end": 169.863,
          "en": "And this can now also be const here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.79,
          "end": 175.38,
          "en": "And then with that, this text is a bit bigger and white.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.38,
          "end": 178.23,
          "en": "Now I'd just like to have more spacing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.23,
          "end": 180.84,
          "en": "between the image and this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.84,
          "end": 184.32,
          "en": "And for that, we have two main ways of doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.32,
          "end": 189.03,
          "en": "The first option is to add some padding on this text button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.03,
          "end": 191.55,
          "en": "which you can do in this styleFrom function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.55,
          "end": 193.26,
          "en": "by setting padding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.26,
          "end": 197.31,
          "en": "Padding simply is some spacing inside of the widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.31,
          "end": 201.3,
          "en": "between the widget content and the widget boundaries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 201.3,
          "end": 204.36,
          "en": "And this padding can be set here for this text button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.36,
          "end": 208.32,
          "en": "with the padding argument in the styleFrom function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.32,
          "end": 212.88,
          "en": "And it wants a edge insets geometry object type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 212.88,
          "end": 214.71,
          "en": "Such an object can be created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.71,
          "end": 218.25,
          "en": "with the edge insets constructor functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.25,
          "end": 220.02,
          "en": "which are suggested to me here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.02,
          "end": 222.3,
          "en": "For example, edge insets all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.3,
          "end": 225.513,
          "en": "adds a certain amount of padding into all directions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.77,
          "end": 229.77,
          "en": "You can also add padding to just the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.77,
          "end": 232.68,
          "en": "by using the only constructor function instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.68,
          "end": 236.94,
          "en": "And there passing the top argument, the named top argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.94,
          "end": 238.68,
          "en": "which then must be set to a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 238.68,
          "end": 240.693,
          "en": "like for example, 20 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.1,
          "end": 244.92,
          "en": "This can also be turned into a constant value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 244.92,
          "end": 246.273,
          "en": "by using const here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 247.83,
          "end": 249.78,
          "en": "And if you do this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.78,
          "end": 252.003,
          "en": "there is more spacing around this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 252.87,
          "end": 254.49,
          "en": "Now the alternative approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 254.49,
          "end": 256.47,
          "en": "to using this padding setting here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 256.47,
          "end": 260.16,
          "en": "which is absolutely fine, I just wanna show you options,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 260.16,
          "end": 264.57,
          "en": "is to comment this out, and instead add an extra widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 264.57,
          "end": 268.11,
          "en": "between the image and the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 268.11,
          "end": 272.07,
          "en": "And that would be the sized box widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.07,
          "end": 274.74,
          "en": "which kind of does what its name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 274.74,
          "end": 278.193,
          "en": "It simply creates a box of a certain size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 279.39,
          "end": 282.63,
          "en": "And you can add a child widget in there if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 282.63,
          "end": 283.71,
          "en": "But most importantly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 283.71,
          "end": 286.26,
          "en": "you can also set a height and a width here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 286.26,
          "end": 289.26,
          "en": "And here we could set this to a height of 20,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 289.26,
          "end": 290.64,
          "en": "and then also add const,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 290.64,
          "end": 293.49,
          "en": "since this can be added for this widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 293.49,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "And that would also add a widget of this size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 298.71,
          "en": "between the image and the button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 298.71,
          "end": 302.22,
          "en": "hence adding this extra spacing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 302.22,
          "end": 304.95,
          "en": "Now we don't see any widget here in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 304.95,
          "end": 307.92,
          "en": "because this sized box doesn't have any content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 307.92,
          "end": 311.1,
          "en": "It's really just a widget of that size, of that height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 311.1,
          "end": 313.05,
          "en": "that just takes up that space",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 313.05,
          "end": 315.24,
          "en": "without showing anything on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 315.24,
          "end": 317.31,
          "en": "And that's also an important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 317.31,
          "end": 319.89,
          "en": "between sized box and other widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 319.89,
          "end": 322.14,
          "en": "like for example, container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 322.14,
          "end": 326.16,
          "en": "Container and most other widgets simply take the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 326.16,
          "end": 328.38,
          "en": "and height they need to take",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 328.38,
          "end": 331.17,
          "en": "to fit their content into themselves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 331.17,
          "end": 334.56,
          "en": "For example, a text widget is just as high and wide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 334.56,
          "end": 337.53,
          "en": "as needed to show the text on the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 337.53,
          "end": 339.78,
          "en": "so that it's not cut off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 339.78,
          "end": 341.73,
          "en": "On the other hand, with sized box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.73,
          "end": 345.21,
          "en": "you explicitly set a certain height or width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 345.21,
          "end": 348.63,
          "en": "and that height or width is then set in stone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 348.63,
          "end": 352.71,
          "en": "If you would have some child widget inside of sized box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 352.71,
          "end": 355.23,
          "en": "that child widget and the content of it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 355.23,
          "end": 359.49,
          "en": "would not lead to sized becoming wider or taller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 359.49,
          "end": 362.07,
          "en": "Sized box has a fixed width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 362.07,
          "end": 364.02,
          "en": "and if it would have some content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 364.02,
          "end": 365.61,
          "en": "that doesn't fit into there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 365.61,
          "end": 368.28,
          "en": "because it, for example, needs more width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 368.28,
          "end": 371.07,
          "en": "that content would be cut off.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 371.07,
          "end": 373.53,
          "en": "And that's an alternative to adding padding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 373.53,
          "end": 375.783,
          "en": "You can use whichever approach you prefer.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
